        "original_id": "bb807138-bdbf-53f9-bfc0-311837608e12",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rufus Wainwright\n- Products: Release the Stars, Going to a Town, Vibrate: The Best of Rufus Wainwright\n- Topics: singles, greatest hits albums, studio releases\n\nFacts:\n- In 1998, Rufus Wainwright released his self-titled debut studio album.\n- In 2001, Rufus Wainwright released the studio album Poses.\n- In 2003, Rufus Wainwright released the studio album Want One.\n- In 2004, Rufus Wainwright released the studio album Want Two.\n- In 2007, Rufus Wainwright released the studio album Release the Stars.\n- Release the Stars generated three singles: \"Going to a Town,\" \"Rules and Regulations,\" and \"Tiergarten.\"\n- \"Going to a Town\" is a song written and performed by Canadian-American singer-songwriter Rufus Wainwright.\n- \"Going to a Town\" peaked at number 54 on the UK Singles Chart.\n- In 2012, Rufus Wainwright released the studio album Out of the Game.\n- The standard edition of Vibrate: The Best of Rufus Wainwright includes eighteen songs from six of Rufus Wainwright's studio releases, plus soundtrack contributions and the previously unreleased track \"Me and Liza.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c51b46a8-b9f7-5af4-b094-d2dfa646e68d",
        "text": "Page: Release the Stars. Sentence: The album generated three singles: \"Going to a Town\", which peaked at number 54 on the UK Singles Chart, \"Rules and Regulations\", and \"Tiergarten\".\nPage: Going to a Town. Sentence: \"Going to a Town\" is a song written and performed by Canadian-American singer-songwriter Rufus Wainwright.\nPage: Vibrate: The Best of Rufus Wainwright. Sentence: The standard issue of the album includes eighteen songs from six of Wainwright's studio releases, including his self-titled debut album (1998), \"Poses\" (2001), \"Want One\" (2003), \"Want Two\" (2004), \"Release the Stars\" (2007) and \"Out of the Game\" (2012), plus soundtrack contributions and one previously unreleased track (\"Me and Liza\").",
